WEBVTT

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:17.130
Nusumareta kako wo

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:20.330
Sagashitsuzukete

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:23.420
Ore wa samayou

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:27.130
Mishiranu machi wo

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:32.080
Honou no nioi shimitsuite

00:00:32.330 --> 00:00:33.880
Museru

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:37.630
Sayonara wa itta hazu da

00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:40.540
Wakareta hazu sa

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:43.790
Jigoku wo mireba

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.330
Kokoro ga kawaku

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:52.750
Tatakai wa akita no sa

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:57.540
Sadame to areba

00:00:57.710 --> 00:01:00.790
Kokoro wo kimeru

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:05.960
Sottoshite oite kure

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:07.750
Ashita ni

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:15.250
Aa tsunagaru kyou gurai

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:55.500
You now know what sort of end
Ypsilon met at Chirico's hands.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:58.880
Is this clear? Do not underestimate him!

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:01.750
We once considered Chirico
an insignificant heretic.

00:02:01.750 --> 00:02:05.630
He has since thrown the Society's
control into the balance.

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:07.710
However, it's too soon to give up!

00:02:08.250 --> 00:02:13.130
We will surround him and
then carefully wait for a chance.

00:02:13.130 --> 00:02:14.960
I will authorize battle only when we have him!

00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:18.080
Wait for my orders before making the final move!

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:20.080
Now go, and may luck be with you!

00:02:22.380 --> 00:02:24.960
Chirico doesn't have an AT, so this should work.

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:26.250
Somehow I doubt it.

00:02:36.130 --> 00:02:38.630
We understand your feelings, Excellency.

00:02:38.630 --> 00:02:42.290
But an excess of caution may not only
give our opponent more time,

00:02:42.290 --> 00:02:44.920
but may let our best chance slip away.

00:02:45.420 --> 00:02:46.670
What are you trying to say?

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:52.130
Those men are the Society's best AT pilots.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:54.750
Your methods couldn't kill Chirico.

00:02:54.750 --> 00:02:57.830
Our failure was in constantly underestimating him!

00:02:57.830 --> 00:03:01.420
Chirico is a man with the battle ability of a PS!

00:03:01.420 --> 00:03:03.290
We recognize that, sir.

00:03:03.290 --> 00:03:06.790
Although we feel you may be
overestimating him now.

00:03:09.130 --> 00:03:11.750
In any case, Chirico is now on Quent.

00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:16.000
And the best data we have on this world is ancient.

00:03:25.460 --> 00:03:30.460
The Desert

00:04:04.420 --> 00:04:05.380
It's sunrise.

00:04:07.130 --> 00:04:08.000
Right...

00:04:26.670 --> 00:04:28.750
Is it always that cold at night here?

00:04:28.750 --> 00:04:29.580
Yes.

00:04:29.920 --> 00:04:32.210
And now it's time for the burning hell, huh?

00:04:32.210 --> 00:04:33.330
Yes.

00:04:34.380 --> 00:04:35.540
What are you doing?

00:04:43.670 --> 00:04:45.540
What's the deal, Shako?

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:50.540
Food. I'm going to catch a sand mole for us.

00:04:51.250 --> 00:04:52.630
Sand mole?

00:04:52.630 --> 00:04:54.000
Don't you have any canned food with you?

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:56.710
Yes, but I don't like it.

00:04:57.420 --> 00:04:58.460
Don't move!

00:05:16.540 --> 00:05:17.790
A lure?

00:05:17.790 --> 00:05:19.880
It sounds like a sand mole's favorite food.

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:22.880
Here it comes.

00:06:24.960 --> 00:06:27.380
Delicious. This can feed us for a month.

00:06:28.380 --> 00:06:30.330
What's wrong? Eat.

00:06:30.330 --> 00:06:31.880
I'm not hungry.

00:06:32.330 --> 00:06:34.330
That's all we'll get until sunset.

00:06:35.130 --> 00:06:37.130
Besides, it's good.

00:06:46.040 --> 00:06:47.790
Guess it's not too bad.

00:06:59.500 --> 00:07:00.830
Are we still far?

00:07:00.830 --> 00:07:02.170
We're almost there.

00:07:02.170 --> 00:07:04.830
How many people are in your village?

00:07:04.830 --> 00:07:06.380
We've never counted.

00:07:07.710 --> 00:07:10.420
Quent's a very strange place.

00:07:10.420 --> 00:07:11.380
You think so?

00:07:21.330 --> 00:07:23.170
How'd the war in Kummen turn out?

00:07:23.170 --> 00:07:26.170
Don't know.
I came back shortly after you escaped.

00:07:26.170 --> 00:07:28.170
Got tired of being a mercenary?

00:07:28.170 --> 00:07:30.080
My contract was terminated.

00:07:30.670 --> 00:07:35.250
It'd take a while to explain, but nothing but
weird things have been happening to me.

00:07:35.250 --> 00:07:37.830
It looks like I may not be a real human after all.

00:07:37.830 --> 00:07:39.500
I may be a PS.

00:07:39.880 --> 00:07:43.290
There are people chasing me because of that.

00:07:46.960 --> 00:07:49.080
Sooner or later, they'll come to this world, too.

00:07:49.750 --> 00:07:51.080
They already have.

00:07:51.460 --> 00:07:52.460
What?

00:07:52.460 --> 00:07:54.880
They appeared in the sky last night.

00:07:54.880 --> 00:07:57.500
Looked like they were doing
some low-orbit surveillance.

00:07:57.500 --> 00:07:58.500
And then?

00:07:58.500 --> 00:08:00.830
And then it got light,
so I couldn't see them anymore.

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:02.880
Don't you sleep at night?

00:08:02.880 --> 00:08:06.420
Quentians don't sleep as much
as you people do.

00:08:19.080 --> 00:08:22.330
We've got ATs shadowing us.
How big is this desert?

00:08:22.750 --> 00:08:24.710
All of Quent is desert.

00:08:24.710 --> 00:08:26.710
There's no place to hide?

00:08:27.080 --> 00:08:30.460
There are villages in the ground crevasses.
We live in them.

00:08:30.460 --> 00:08:32.580
Shako, where's the nearest crevasse?

00:08:32.580 --> 00:08:33.670
Not far.

00:08:34.630 --> 00:08:35.830
Any escorts around them?

00:08:35.830 --> 00:08:38.750
None, but I think they've spotted us.

00:08:39.170 --> 00:08:42.210
No metallic objects detected
within a 2 kilometer radius.

00:08:42.210 --> 00:08:43.670
Try to provoke them.

00:08:43.670 --> 00:08:44.670
Roger!

00:08:49.420 --> 00:08:51.250
They want to fight. One of them's moving in.

00:08:51.250 --> 00:08:53.540
It's coming around in front! Shako, any weapons?

00:08:53.540 --> 00:08:54.710
Just my spear.

00:09:05.290 --> 00:09:06.630
They still haven't changed course.

00:09:06.630 --> 00:09:07.460
Distance?

00:09:07.460 --> 00:09:08.580
300...

00:09:08.580 --> 00:09:09.830
270...

00:09:10.170 --> 00:09:11.330
250...

00:09:11.330 --> 00:09:12.580
Try firing off some rounds.

00:09:12.580 --> 00:09:13.290
Roger!

00:09:40.500 --> 00:09:42.500
They changed course!

00:09:42.500 --> 00:09:44.170
No counterattack?

00:09:44.170 --> 00:09:46.170
No, they just avoided us.

00:09:46.170 --> 00:09:49.170
They're continuing on, speed unchanged.

00:09:50.330 --> 00:09:53.830
Looks like there's no problem.
Shall we commence a full attack?

00:09:54.080 --> 00:09:57.290
Don't forget, he has a Quentman with him.

00:09:57.630 --> 00:10:03.170
But, sir, is having one Quentian
involved that great a risk?

00:10:03.170 --> 00:10:06.000
We are in Quentian airspace.

00:10:06.290 --> 00:10:10.460
Are you saying they'll shoot this vessel down?

00:10:10.460 --> 00:10:15.500
The pathetic Quentians, who lost their civilization
and have to earn their living as hired soldiers?

00:10:15.500 --> 00:10:17.540
They were a great people, long ago.

00:10:17.540 --> 00:10:19.420
And now they're not.

00:10:20.130 --> 00:10:21.580
In your opinion!

00:10:21.580 --> 00:10:27.040
It's a fact that they once had the power
to control the entire Astragius galaxy!

00:10:28.330 --> 00:10:29.750
Very well, sir.

00:10:32.710 --> 00:10:36.750
Here are your orders:
Stop them, but do not use your weapons.

00:10:37.080 --> 00:10:39.790
Separate Chirico from the Quentian!

00:10:39.790 --> 00:10:40.630
Understood?

00:10:40.630 --> 00:10:41.630
Roger!

00:10:55.130 --> 00:10:56.500
Shako, go faster!

00:10:56.500 --> 00:10:58.290
This sandrunner isn't built for efficiency.

00:10:58.290 --> 00:11:00.000
We just have to go straight!

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:02.630
If we go faster, it'll eat too much fuel.

00:11:02.630 --> 00:11:05.580
We still have a ways to go,
but the crevasse is near.

00:11:19.040 --> 00:11:19.790
Shako!

00:11:19.790 --> 00:11:20.630
We're almost there.

00:11:35.830 --> 00:11:37.330
Shako, go faster!

00:11:37.330 --> 00:11:38.420
Almost there...

00:12:36.330 --> 00:12:37.670
Do you hear anything?

00:12:39.210 --> 00:12:41.250
Don't you have a metal detection radar unit?

00:12:41.250 --> 00:12:43.580
I thought Quent made the best ones.

00:12:43.830 --> 00:12:44.750
I don't.

00:12:54.960 --> 00:12:58.080
And why is there a road in a place like this?

00:12:58.380 --> 00:13:02.210
Quentians built it. There's a village down there.

00:13:02.210 --> 00:13:03.380
Any friends here?

00:13:03.380 --> 00:13:04.920
I don't know this village.

00:13:04.920 --> 00:13:07.170
Let's go down. They must have weapons.

00:13:07.830 --> 00:13:09.380
No, they wouldn't.

00:13:09.380 --> 00:13:12.080
Quentians don't fight on this world.

00:13:18.420 --> 00:13:19.540
What's wrong?

00:13:20.250 --> 00:13:23.330
Looks like that last guy wrecked the radiator.

00:13:23.330 --> 00:13:24.750
Any chance you can fix it?

00:13:25.330 --> 00:13:26.500
Dunno.

00:13:35.130 --> 00:13:36.880
There's no sign of them.

00:13:37.460 --> 00:13:39.960
We believe they probably fell into the crevasse.

00:13:39.960 --> 00:13:44.460
But, if they're still alive, they may be following
a road down to the valley floor.

00:13:44.460 --> 00:13:47.960
That crevasse probably contains
a Quentian village.

00:13:47.960 --> 00:13:51.250
It makes no difference.
What we're after is Chirico.

00:13:51.250 --> 00:13:53.290
Are we going to inform His Excellency?

00:13:55.290 --> 00:13:58.210
A good subordinate doesn't disturb
his commander's sleep.

00:13:59.290 --> 00:14:00.630
Continue the investigation!

00:14:00.630 --> 00:14:02.880
You're authorized to open fire
if the situation demands it!

00:14:02.880 --> 00:14:04.170
Aye, sir!

00:14:04.960 --> 00:14:06.080
We've no other choice.

00:14:06.080 --> 00:14:06.830
Quite right.

00:14:18.920 --> 00:14:20.210
I don't understand.

00:14:20.210 --> 00:14:21.420
Understand what?

00:14:23.330 --> 00:14:24.580
Anything.

00:14:24.580 --> 00:14:27.580
How can Quent have a 3,000 year history
of producing mercenaries,

00:14:27.580 --> 00:14:29.460
and yet its villages don't have any weapons?

00:14:29.460 --> 00:14:31.960
And what do you mean you people don't fight?

00:14:31.960 --> 00:14:35.000
No decent communication or
transportation facilities...

00:14:35.000 --> 00:14:36.630
This is Quent?

00:14:36.630 --> 00:14:38.380
It's just a primitive backwater!

00:14:38.380 --> 00:14:39.710
Does that upset you?

00:14:40.000 --> 00:14:43.000
No... It's just that it isn't what I had pictured.

00:14:43.330 --> 00:14:45.790
It isn't like we have no mechanical conveniences.

00:14:45.790 --> 00:14:47.500
It's just that most people choose not to use them.

00:14:47.880 --> 00:14:51.750
When I became a mercenary, I knew
from the beginning how to use machinery.

00:14:51.750 --> 00:14:55.380
But most Quentians
know nothing of the outside world.

00:15:17.380 --> 00:15:19.500
The village is right below us.

00:15:19.670 --> 00:15:21.420
How far down is it?

00:15:21.420 --> 00:15:23.540
Around 1000 meters or so.

00:15:23.920 --> 00:15:26.880
Down there it doesn't get too hot or too cold.

00:15:26.880 --> 00:15:28.670
You live like sand moles.

00:15:28.670 --> 00:15:30.670
Do you know what the word "Quent" means?

00:15:30.670 --> 00:15:31.500
No.

00:15:31.500 --> 00:15:33.460
"The bottom of the valley."

00:15:33.460 --> 00:15:37.250
Quentians are born and die
in the crevasses' depths.

00:15:37.250 --> 00:15:38.080
Help me.

00:15:38.420 --> 00:15:39.330
Right.

00:16:08.420 --> 00:16:10.420
No choice. We'll have to floor it,
even if it is broken.

00:16:10.420 --> 00:16:11.080
Gotcha!

00:16:14.710 --> 00:16:16.750
After them! B-Group, take the opposite side!

00:16:16.750 --> 00:16:18.460
C-Group, wait for them on the surface!

00:16:18.460 --> 00:16:19.540
Do we open fire?

00:16:19.540 --> 00:16:20.670
Doesn't matter!

00:16:41.080 --> 00:16:42.580
Shako, what about the village below us?

00:16:43.420 --> 00:16:45.040
Probably destroyed.

00:17:08.500 --> 00:17:13.500
Strange to think that the only two guys
to survive Kummen would die so easily.

00:17:13.500 --> 00:17:15.170
Are you giving up?

00:17:16.170 --> 00:17:18.500
We have no other weapons
and our ammo's running out.

00:17:18.500 --> 00:17:20.670
You've really changed.

00:17:20.670 --> 00:17:23.420
The old Chirico would never be so pessimistic.

00:17:24.170 --> 00:17:28.210
We don't have a word for it in Quentinese,
but you seem... softer , now.

00:17:29.500 --> 00:17:30.460
Disappointed?

00:17:31.170 --> 00:17:32.170
No.

00:17:34.040 --> 00:17:36.170
I like you much better this way.

00:17:46.210 --> 00:17:48.170
You're trapped like rats in a bag!

00:17:48.170 --> 00:17:50.750
We know you have no weapons!
Surrender peacefully!

00:17:50.750 --> 00:17:52.830
Otherwise, we'll open fire on you!

00:17:53.540 --> 00:17:55.460
Will you surrender without a fight?

00:17:55.460 --> 00:17:57.460
No, I still have some surprises left.

00:17:57.460 --> 00:17:59.580
This is the only way to cause a diversion.

00:17:59.580 --> 00:18:03.130
And, unlike in Kummen,
we've only got five ATs to deal with here.

00:18:03.630 --> 00:18:06.750
Maybe you really haven't changed that much.

00:18:07.210 --> 00:18:08.880
Neither of us has.

00:18:08.880 --> 00:18:11.880
If you don't come out, we'll open fire on you!

00:18:13.210 --> 00:18:15.290
Shako, I'll draw their fire!

00:19:02.830 --> 00:19:04.500
You're still alive? Are you all right?

00:19:04.830 --> 00:19:06.460
Yeah, I'm fine.

00:19:07.330 --> 00:19:08.830
Who... who are you?

00:20:16.330 --> 00:20:17.960
Looks like we made it.

00:20:17.960 --> 00:20:18.960
Yeah.

00:20:28.040 --> 00:20:32.500
So, he took out five ATs
and now has one for himself?

00:20:34.920 --> 00:20:39.710
Uh, well, at least we have proof
that they have no other weapons.

00:20:39.710 --> 00:20:42.000
Now that they're back in the desert,
we have a chance.

00:20:42.000 --> 00:20:43.960
Give the order to attack, sir!

00:20:43.960 --> 00:20:49.880
Silence! Your biggest mistake was
letting them fight near a Quentian village!

00:20:50.040 --> 00:20:53.000
Yes! What's done is done!

00:20:53.000 --> 00:20:55.380
Exactly, so we may as well... You know?

00:20:55.380 --> 00:20:59.880
Idiots! You defied my orders and caused all this!

00:20:59.880 --> 00:21:01.380
Never mind! Just get out of my sight!

00:21:01.380 --> 00:21:02.750
Ye... Yes, sir!

00:21:03.920 --> 00:21:05.920
If you'll excuse us.

00:21:14.960 --> 00:21:18.670
They're being too sloppy in dealing with this world!

00:21:27.080 --> 00:21:28.750
It's a damned shame.

00:21:28.750 --> 00:21:31.880
We lost a month's worth of food
down that crevasse.

00:21:34.960 --> 00:21:39.170
Tell me, Shako. Do you think I'm really a PS?

00:21:40.080 --> 00:21:41.290
A PS?

00:21:41.790 --> 00:21:43.040
Well now...

00:21:43.040 --> 00:21:45.630
You're definitely not an ordinary man.

00:22:14.130 --> 00:22:15.250
There it is.

00:22:24.420 --> 00:22:27.500
The Quentian village lay
in the depths of the ground.

00:22:28.460 --> 00:22:33.670
But was the mystery of the PS,
of my own origins, hidden here?

00:22:36.040 --> 00:22:38.880
A race which had abandoned civilization
and destroyed itself.

00:22:40.290 --> 00:22:44.500
Wasn't Quent, in the end, simply a graveyard?

00:22:54.290 --> 00:22:55.710
Next Episode

00:22:56.130 --> 00:22:58.960
"Quent" means "the bottom of the valley."

00:22:58.960 --> 00:23:00.500
Crossing thousands of years,

00:23:00.500 --> 00:23:03.830
pursuing the remains of a super civilization
hidden in the depths of the ground,

00:23:03.830 --> 00:23:05.580
Chirico runs onward.

00:23:06.170 --> 00:23:07.710
Who were the gods of Quent?

00:23:07.710 --> 00:23:09.540
What were the ambitions of the Children of God?

00:23:09.920 --> 00:23:15.670
Chirico wanders the smoky valley,
seeking the roots of his past.

00:23:16.330 --> 00:23:18.330
Next time, "Legacy"

00:23:18.880 --> 00:23:21.630
Chirico is both the hunter and the hunted.

00:23:19.790 --> 00:23:24.290
Legacy

00:23:19.790 --> 00:23:24.290
Next Time

00:23:42.540 --> 00:23:46.000
Samishii toki mo

00:23:46.000 --> 00:23:49.540
Kanashii toki mo

00:23:49.540 --> 00:23:55.920
Itsumo anata ga me ni ukabu

00:23:56.420 --> 00:23:59.960
Hitori no toki mo

00:23:59.960 --> 00:24:03.380
Aitai toki mo

00:24:03.380 --> 00:24:09.630
Itsumo anata wa mune no naka

00:24:09.630 --> 00:24:13.130
Tooku hanarete itemo

00:24:13.130 --> 00:24:16.540
Tatoe wakarete itemo

00:24:16.710 --> 00:24:23.040
Kono yo no hikari to tomo ni mabushiku

00:24:23.420 --> 00:24:29.380
Ano hi no anata ga...
